-/// An input region needs no pointer. Returns whether it was applied.
+/// An input region needs no pointer, so this works on native Wayland too.
+/// Returns whether it was applied.
+///
+/// The region is the window widget's (as tao's own call sets it), not its
+/// GDK window's: GTK sets the GDK window's input shape again from the
+/// widget's (cut to its client-side decoration) each time that decoration
+/// changes, on a resize or when the window is shown again, and on Wayland
+/// that put back the whole window, so a locked meter took the mouse again
+/// as soon as it grew a row. And Wayland gets a new input region only with
+/// the window's next frame, so one is drawn at once: an idle window stayed
+/// clickable until something on it changed.
 ///
 /// A window `hide_in_place` hid never takes the mouse, whatever asks: it is
 /// invisible but still there, and took every click over it once a screenshot
 /// tool left the front (`screenshot_tool` gives every window the mouse back).
+/// What it is told meanwhile is kept for `reveal_in_place`.
